Z||000000||DR650SE||11-15-2001||10:53 AM||||       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> Lesson of the day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><BR>Don't downshift and engine brake when comming around a turn fast, esspecially when slightly damp.  I did this on my way out of school on a down hill road with enough room for one may be two small cars and curbs on both sides.  I almost lost the back end.  Being the slick driver I am,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I worked it out with no damage or contact with the curbs and just looked like the man.  Wont be doing that again.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||12
Z||000001||DR650SE||11-15-2001||03:22 PM||||Anyone every do this or have the same experiance or is it just me?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||11-15-2001||05:10 PM||||Not enough experience/time driven in my recent-acquired Fiero to have that just yet.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But I DID have a few turning fast and always caught the back end when it started to slip.  (But one of these days I'm gonna lose the fight  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">) But downshifting when turning fast, haven't done that.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_cdn.JPG">   </A>  <BR>AIM: CanadianFiero<p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||11-15-2001||05:30 PM||||Gotta have the Fiero in the right gear going into the corner so you can power out.  Drop throttle oversteer is the leading cause of lost control in high speed corners in a Fiero.<P>The car has high limits, but to use those limits, the car demands you drive it the way IT wants to be driven. ||||reg||6
Z||000004||DR650SE||11-15-2001||05:57 PM||||Formula, your completly right.  I just like to goof off sometimes. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||11-15-2001||09:00 PM||||In almost any car, decelerating while cornering hard will make the rear want to come unstuck.  It's a physics thing: deceleration transfers weight forward, which makes the front tires stick better and the rear tires stick less.  (Yeah, my grammar stinks.)  Also, when you engine-brake, you're asking the rear tires to do more work; they can do only so much.  On top of that, Fieros are a little butt-heavy; when you get one unstuck, the heavy end tries to lead.  And the '84-'87 rear suspension toes-out on rebound, causing bump steer.  The combination can be scary.  Nice save!<P>All that sounds terrible, but some other cars are much worse, <I>e.g.</I> old swing-axle Volkswagens, Porsches, Fiat 850's, and Triumph Spitfires.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||The Fieromaster||11-15-2001||09:25 PM||||Thats it im gonna drive over your house and smack ya! Lol.. j/k!   Yea its bad i you let off the gas in a hard turn to man... ALthough you can use that teqniuqe (sp??) to drift the car!<BR>Hope to see you out cruisin to night man!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">         <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">      <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                 <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||11-15-2001||09:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DR650SE:<BR><B>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif">  Lesson of the day   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> <BR>Don't downshift and engine brake when comming around a turn fast, esspecially when slightly damp.  I did this on my way out of school on a down hill road with enough room for one may be two small cars and curbs on both sides.  I almost lost the back end.  Being the slick driver I am,   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I worked it out with no damage or contact with the curbs and just looked like the man.  Wont be doing that again.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's fun on the wet stuff, but I have fun dropping from fifth to third and dropping the hammer on dry roads, it also makes the rear swing out...<BR>Depending on your suspension and experience, you can feather the gas to keep it sideways, or let off and straighten out...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||11-16-2001||01:09 AM||||Heel and Toe...  <P>Heel and Toe...  <P>Heel and Toe...<P>It's not a dance (well, it rather is, actually, but not that kind...) It's THE way to keep your car on the road, out of the reeds  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||Spektrum-87GT||11-16-2001||05:53 PM||||the car has insane limits... but dont cross them!!! i learned the hard way... but i dont feel bad, seems like it happens a lot!||||reg||1
Z||000010||johnt671||11-16-2001||09:01 PM||||I did it last month.  I had to get new tires as my old performance tires wouldn't pass inspection.  Went around a turn like I did on the old tires and got 1/3 sideways befor I caught it.  The guy at the tire shop talked me into Goodyear Wingfoots.  No good ,to hard.  Went back and told him if anyone askes, they are a pos for the way I drive.  He offered to swap them for me but I had to many miles on them. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Phil||11-16-2001||10:47 PM||||NEVER unload the chassis in a corner. Come out of a turn in the same gear as you entered||||reg||1
Z||000012||3.8T Fiero GT||11-18-2001||03:57 AM||||nice save!<P>drifting is SO fun...they do it in RWD drive cars in japan SO much and those are front engine cars, so even more sway!  but i so luv it in the Fiero, i cant wait to have more power under my foot to try!!!<P>BUT as for track driving...u can ONLY do one thing at a time, either accelerate, brake or turn. - never two at the same time or this can cause something quite unwanted!!! as I have learned from others at Cayuga & Shannonville.  this technique is considered proper...yet drifting cancels out these rules and is just fun!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cache.ucr.edu/~currie/turbo-t.jpg">  <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B>||||reg||1
